{"title":"Career Roadmap · Automotive Embedded Engineer","role":"Automotive Embedded Engineer","summary":"An Automotive Embedded Engineer develops the software and electronics that control and monitor modern vehicles.","facts":{"Current degree":"B.Tech / B.E. (Bachelor of Technology / Engineering)","Course":"Automotive Electronics / Autonomous Vehicles"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Career Overview"},{"type":"p","text":"An Automotive Embedded Engineer develops the software and electronics that control and monitor modern vehicles."},{"type":"p","text":"The role sits at the intersection of:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Embedded systems"},{"text":"Electronics"},{"text":"Automotive engineering"},{"text":"C/C++"},{"text":"Microcontrollers"},{"text":"Real-time operating systems"},{"text":"Automotive communication"},{"text":"Sensors"},{"text":"Control systems"},{"text":"Functional safety"},{"text":"Autonomous driving"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Automotive embedded engineers may work on:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Engine and powertrain control"},{"text":"Body electronics"},{"text":"Infotainment"},{"text":"ADAS"},{"text":"Battery-management systems"},{"text":"Electric vehicles"},{"text":"Vehicle networking"},{"text":"Instrument clusters"},{"text":"Autonomous-driving systems"},{"text":"Automotive cybersecurity"},{"text":"Vehicle control units (ECUs)"}]},{"type":"p","text":"The field is moving from conventional ECU programming toward software-defined vehicles, where vehicles increasingly behave like complex distributed computing platforms."}]},{"heading":"Career Horizons","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Period","Career Focus","Expected Development"],"rows":[[{"text":"2026–2030"},{"text":"Embedded Foundation"},{"text":"C/C++, microcontrollers, electronics, RTOS, automotive protocols"}],[{"text":"2030–2035"},{"text":"Automotive Embedded Engineer"},{"text":"ECU d